---
import PortfolioLayout from '../../layouts/PortfolioLayout.astro';
---
<PortfolioLayout view="what-i-do" title="What I do · Ilias Ennajmi" description="Brand strategy, campaigns, marketing systems and behavioural insight, and how I work on each.">
  <div class="gut"><div class="wrap">
    <header class="grid page-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">What I do · how I work</span>
      <h1 class="display">What I do, <em>and how.</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">Four things people hire me for, what changes when I'm in the room, and how to get the best out of me.</p>
    </header>

    <div>
      <div class="sec-head"><span class="label">What I'm hired for</span><span class="label">Tap one to open it</span></div>
      <details class="svc" open>
        <summary><span class="obj"><img class="o-compass" src="/portfolio/img/compass.webp" alt="A chrome compass" loading="lazy"></span><span class="t">Brand strategy</span><span class="d">Where the brand stands, who it's for, and the one thing it says.</span><span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="more"><div class="get"><span class="label">What you get</span><ul><li>A positioning you can say in one sentence</li><li>The customer tension the brand resolves</li><li>A message house the whole team can write from</li><li>A creative brief that's ready to use</li></ul></div><div class="when"><div><span class="label">Good when</span><p>You're launching, repositioning, or everyone in the company describes the brand differently.</p></div><div><span class="label">Typical time</span><p>Three to six weeks.</p></div></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="svc">
        <summary><span class="obj"><img class="o-hook" src="/portfolio/img/hook.webp" alt="A chrome fishing hook" loading="lazy"></span><span class="t">Campaigns</span><span class="d">One idea, carried across every channel it needs.</span><span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="more"><div class="get"><span class="label">What you get</span><ul><li>A campaign platform and the line that carries it</li><li>A channel plan built around how people decide</li><li>A strategist in the room through production</li><li>A read-out afterwards: what moved and what didn't</li></ul></div><div class="when"><div><span class="label">Good when</span><p>You have a launch date, a budget and too many ideas, or none.</p></div><div><span class="label">Typical time</span><p>Four to ten weeks.</p></div></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="svc">
        <summary><span class="obj"><img class="o-gears" src="/portfolio/img/gears.webp" alt="Chrome gears" loading="lazy"></span><span class="t">Marketing systems</span><span class="d">The machine that keeps working after the campaign ends.</span><span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="more"><div class="get"><span class="label">What you get</span><ul><li>A content engine and a calendar people keep to</li><li>Lifecycle and CRM flows, from welcome to win-back</li><li>Automation and AI workflows for the repetitive work</li><li>A dashboard the team actually reads</li></ul></div><div class="when"><div><span class="label">Good when</span><p>Marketing depends on heroics, and stops when one person goes on holiday.</p></div><div><span class="label">Typical time</span><p>Four to eight weeks, then a handover.</p></div></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="svc">
        <summary><span class="obj"><img class="o-magnet" src="/portfolio/img/magnet.webp" alt="A chrome magnet" loading="lazy"></span><span class="t">Behavioural insight</span><span class="d">Why people choose, stall, or quietly leave.</span><span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
        <div class="more"><div class="get"><span class="label">What you get</span><ul><li>Customer interviews and field notes</li><li>A map of the decision: defaults, friction, anchors</li><li>A short list of tests worth running</li><li>Findings on one page</li></ul></div><div class="when"><div><span class="label">Good when</span><p>The numbers say what is happening and nobody can say why.</p></div><div><span class="label">Typical time</span><p>Two to four weeks.</p></div></div></div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="sec band">
      <div class="sec-head"><span class="label">What changes when I'm in the room</span><span class="label">Before → after</span></div>
      <div class="value">
        <div class="vrow"><span class="from">A list of twelve features</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="to">One reason to choose you.</span></div>
        <div class="vrow"><span class="from">Ten opinions in a meeting</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="to">One sentence everybody can repeat.</span></div>
        <div class="vrow"><span class="from">"We think customers want…"</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="to">"Twelve customers told us…"</span></div>
        <div class="vrow"><span class="from">A campaign that ends in June</span><span class="arr">→</span><span class="to">A system still running in December.</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sec">
      <div class="sec-head"><span class="label">How I work</span><span class="label">Five steps, every brief</span></div>
      <div class="grid how">
        <div class="badge-col">
          <div class="lanyard" id="lanyard" aria-label="Staff badge">
            <img src="/portfolio/img/badge.webp" alt="" draggable="false" loading="lazy">
            <div class="idcard">
              <h4>The <em>Strategist</em></h4>
              <div class="sub"><b>Access</b> all rooms</div>
              <div class="ph"><img src="/portfolio/img/portrait.webp" alt="" loading="lazy"></div>
              <dl><div><dt>Name</dt><dd>Ilias Ennajmi</dd></div><div><dt>Base</dt><dd>Casablanca</dd></div></dl>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ol class="steps steps-col">
          <li><span class="n">(1)</span><span class="k">Ride along</span><p>I meet the customers before I meet the deck. Calls, shops, comment sections, the queue.</p></li>
          <li><span class="n">(2)</span><span class="k">Find the tension</span><p>The thing people feel and nobody says. That's where the idea is hiding.</p></li>
          <li><span class="n">(3)</span><span class="k">Bet on one line</span><p>One insight, written as one sentence, defended in the room.</p></li>
          <li><span class="n">(4)</span><span class="k">Make it together</span><p>Workshops with the creative team. Kill fast, rebuild, keep what survives.</p></li>
          <li><span class="n">(5)</span><span class="k">Read the meters</span><p>What moved, what didn't, and what we'd change next time.</p></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sec">
      <div class="leaflet">
        <div class="leaflet-head"><h3>Instructions <em>for use</em></h3><span class="label">Read before working<br>with Ilias Ennajmi</span></div>
        <div class="leaflet-cols">
          <div><h4>Dosage</h4><p>Start with one 90-minute conversation. No deck, no brief yet. Just the problem.</p></div>
          <div><h4>Feed with</h4><p>Real customers, real numbers, and the complaint emails nobody forwards.</p></div>
          <div><h4>Storage</h4><p>Keep close to the creative team. Works badly when stored in a separate building.</p></div>
          <div><h4>Do not</h4><p>Expose to 80-slide decks. Do not use to decorate a decision that's already made.</p></div>
          <div><h4>Side effects</h4><p>Fewer meetings. Shorter briefs. Occasional uncomfortable questions.</p></div>
          <div><h4>If symptoms persist</h4><p>Say so early. I'd rather hear "no" on Tuesday than "hmm" on Friday.</p></div>
          <div><h4>Contains</h4><p>Persuasion. Does not contain tricks people would be angry to discover.</p></div>
        </div>
        <img class="stamp leaflet-stamp" src="/portfolio/img/stamp_ask.webp" alt="Stamp: Ask why first" loading="lazy" width="700" height="156">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</PortfolioLayout>
